<newsitem itemid="28009" id="root" date="1996-09-02" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Burmah H1 net income rises 13 pct.</title>
<headline>Burmah H1 net income rises 13 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		32.8		   vs 29.7</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 12.0		   vs 11.0</p>
<p> Attributable net income 67.7		  vs 59.9</p>
<p> Exceptional gains	23.2		   vs nil</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on net income before exceptional items were in a range of 60 to 70 million stg. The exceptional gains stem from the sale of fuels operations earlier this year.  </p>
<p> Pretax profit	    125.9		  vs 117.1</p>
<p> Turnover		   1,529		  vs 1,528</p>
<p> Operating profit	 136.6		  vs 130.8</p>
<p> Interest		   10.7 debit	   vs 13.7 debit</p>
<p> Tax			  53.4		   vs 47.0</p>
<p>Breakdown of operating profit -  Lubricants		 100.8		  vs 94.3</p>
<p> Chemicals		  32.2		   vs 30.0</p>
<p> Fuels			0.9 loss	     vs 2.2 profit</p>
<p> LNG			  3.6		    vs 2.9</p>
<p> Pay date		   Jan 10, 1997</p>
<p>Div registration date  Oct 15  Ex-div date		Oct 7</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
